UPDATE tp_questions q JOIN tp_exams e ON e.exam_id = q.exam_id SET q.body_text = 'Man: We usually treat price as a simple scoreboard of supply and demand, but there is a whole class of goods where the high price is itself part of the appeal. — Woman: You mean diamonds and handbags that cost more than their materials could ever explain? — Man: Exactly. Thorstein Veblen argued in 1899 that people sometimes buy things precisely because they are expensive, since the price broadcasts that the owner can afford to waste money. — Woman: So demand can rise with price — raise the price and some buyers want it more. — Man: That is the odd part. Standard theory says a price rise thins the queue, but with these goods a price rise can leave the queue longer, because a cheaper version quietly stops being worth buying.' WHERE e.exam_code = 'TP-PRACTICE-2026-SET08' AND q.order_no = 90;
